# Without types the field holds a string. The switch asks whether it is a rope, reads its length once, and compares the characters only with the cases of that length:
# "circle" and "square" are six characters, each compared as one 48-bit constant. No case is looked up in a table of strings, and no string is compared by a call into the run time.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="areaOf" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[kind]] = Load(b@[[shape]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[text]] = Load(b@[[kind]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:JSRopeString_fiber0)
# CHECK: Int32 b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[text]], offset = 4, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:StringImpl_length)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[hasSixCharacters]] = Equal(b@{{*}}, $6(
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[hasSixCharacters]], Terminal)
# CHECK: Patchpoint(b@[[kind]]:Register({{*}}), $111516199315811(b@{{*}}):Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = WarmAny, Terminal|ControlDependent
# CHECK: Patchpoint(b@[[kind]]:Register({{*}}), $111541935763827(b@{{*}}):Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = WarmAny, Terminal|ControlDependent
# Inside a case the object is asked for its shape before a field of that case is read.
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[shapeWord]] = Load(b@[[shape]], offset = 12, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:AOTObject_shapeWord, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[shape]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
